# The sum of two balls with 2-limb centers: the center by add_2_2, whose error is at most U |cz|
# with U = unit_computed(add_2_2); its bound has no underflow term, so there is no V term.
kernel:        ball_add_2
input:         cx = cx0 cx1
input:         stored rx
input:         cy = cy0 cy1
input:         stored ry
output:        cz = cz0 cz1
output:        rz
value:         cx+cy
requires:      normalized cx
requires:      nonneg rx
requires:      normalized cy
requires:      nonneg ry
ensures:       normalized cz
ensures:       encloses cz rz x+y x=cx,rx y=cy,ry
min_precision: 3
theorem:       proofs/theories/Ball.v ball_add_2_correct
source:        midpoint-radius sum (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

(cz0, cz1) = add_2_2(cx0, cx1, cy0, cy1)
mz         = abs_upper_2(cz0, cz1)
d          = rmul(const unit_computed(add_2_2), mz)
r0         = radd(rx, ry)
rz         = radd(r0, d)
